<title>SOUTH KOREA: Bank of Korea buys dollars at 888.60 won - dealers.</title>
<headline>Bank of Korea buys dollars at 888.60 won - dealers.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-06-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of Korea intervened in Seoul's interbank market at mid-morning on Monday, buying dollars at 888.60 won to slow the won's rise, dealers said.</p>
<p>Officials at the central bank were not immediately available for comment.  </p>
<p>The won was trading at 889.00 at 0140 GMT, down from a session high of 888.60 won.</p>
<p>The currency opened trading at 889.50 and briefly touched a low of 890.00.</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727-5646</p>
</text>
